WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.168
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:02.969
We're here with
Congresswoman Ocasio-Cortez.

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.203
So I feel like for two years

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:05.738
we talked about
who's going to win the House.

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:08.608
And then for weeks we covered
who's going to be the Speaker.

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:12.345
And then since Kevin McCarthy
got the gavel, I -- nothing.

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.846
I feel like we
barely hear anything.

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:15.782
For someone
who's up close to it,

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:20.085
what do you feel the GOP
is trying to do with this power?

00:00:20.085 --> 00:00:23.690
-Yeah, well, first of all,
you're absolutely right.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:28.728
I believe this is the least
productive first three months

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.464
under almost any Speaker

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.898
potentially in the history
of the United States,

00:00:32.898 --> 00:00:35.167
if not in modern
political history.

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:37.370
And I think it's because,
you know,

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.039
they talked a lot
about winning,

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:44.010
but they didn't really plan
for what they wanted to do.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.445
So they're kind of
sitting around

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:47.580
and they're looking
at state legislatures

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.049
and they're like,
"Maybe we can ban books."

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:55.054
And we say, "No,
you should not do that."

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:58.958
And I think
they're, you know --

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:02.027
I'm so grateful that we have
a Democratic Senate

00:01:02.027 --> 00:01:03.362
and that folks turned out

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:06.131
and elected so many incredible
members of the Senate

00:01:06.131 --> 00:01:08.334
to be a kind
of a stop on that.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.935
But I just think
they don't really know.

00:01:09.935 --> 00:01:12.972
And I also think Kevin McCarthy
promised so many people

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:17.776
so many different things
that he cannot possibly govern

00:01:17.776 --> 00:01:20.446
with all these pre-commitments
that he's made.

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:24.350
-A way to, I guess,
seem like you're doing something

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.253
while also not governing
is to complain about wokeism

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.455
and how it affects
everything from bank

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:32.959
collapses to the way
our military is being run.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:37.330
Is that -- Are you in actual
meetings and committee hearings

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.598
where that is the sort of
topic du jour?

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:41.300
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:45.905
House Republicans held an
entire -- an entire hearing

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:49.275
on "wokeism"
in the federal government

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.944
and federal employment policies.
And so I'm looking at it.

00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:55.048
I'm like, "What is so woke
that has them so outraged?"

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:56.549
And I look through this list
and I'm like,

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:59.886
oh, paying members
of the Forest Service

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:02.589
more than a Walmart greeter,

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:05.191
using remote work
for people with disabilities

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.992
and people who live
in rural areas,

00:02:06.992 --> 00:02:08.995
you know, healthcare,

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:13.232
and like --
it's just a catch-all term

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:14.867
that they use for anything
that they don't like.

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:16.268
-And I guess
one of the problems

00:02:16.268 --> 00:02:18.971
is when they actually get to
legislating on things like that,

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:20.372
even their constituents

00:02:20.372 --> 00:02:22.542
wouldn't want to lose things
like healthcare,

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:24.476
especially when
they realize wokeism

00:02:24.476 --> 00:02:25.578
has nothing to do with it.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:26.812
-Yeah, I think
that's why they have to

00:02:26.812 --> 00:02:28.280
call it wokeism

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.783
because if they actually told
their constituents,

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:34.720
"Hey, we don't want the Forest
Service folks to get paid well,"

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.922
people would be like,
"Why do you want to do that?"

00:02:36.922 --> 00:02:41.260
And so I think they have to
brand it as all this stuff.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.362
And I mean,
they'll say it often.

00:02:43.362 --> 00:02:46.232
I was on the floor of a debate
around some of their work

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:50.837
in trying to ban books and they
call it "parental rights"

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:54.874
but they try to package this
and use misdirection

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:57.210
to say "we want parents
to be more involved

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.577
and have more of a say
in their school."

00:02:58.577 --> 00:03:02.248
Well, if you want that,
maybe let's create a society

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:03.983
where parents aren't working
two jobs

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.484
so that they can be
more involved

00:03:05.484 --> 00:03:06.753
with their kids in school.

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:08.421
[ Applause ]

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:12.959
Instead of trying
to tell people

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:17.229
that trans kids should not have
a safe place to get an education

00:03:17.229 --> 00:03:18.898
or tell their parents
what to do.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:22.735
I mean, it's, you know,
I think it speaks to the fact

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:25.638
that despite no matter
what happens with Donald Trump,

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:29.575
Trumpism is still alive.
And we've seen it recently.

00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:31.244
There was just a vote

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:34.914
in the Tennessee
state legislature to expel

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:39.318
three Democratic representatives
in their legislature

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:43.088
because they had the audacity
to stand up and protest

00:03:43.088 --> 00:03:44.423
for gun-safety legislation

00:03:44.423 --> 00:03:47.092
because the state of Tennessee
was not acting enough.

00:03:47.092 --> 00:03:50.829
And so instead
of having vigorous debate,

00:03:50.829 --> 00:03:53.833
the folks who accuse people
of silencing

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:56.202
are the ones who are silencing
and expelling.

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:59.271
The folks who are accusing
people of intimidation,

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:01.874
like Marjorie
Taylor Greene today.

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:03.542
You know, we have --
New York City Public Advocate

00:04:03.542 --> 00:04:05.778
Jumaane Williams is blowing
a whistle while she was talking.

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.914
I mean, we all have our First
Amendment right, right?

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:10.817
She goes around
calling this intimidation.

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:14.386
And it's so often
this politics of projection

00:04:14.386 --> 00:04:16.856
in order to get you
to become defensive

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:20.025
about what this person --
defensive towards yourself

00:04:20.025 --> 00:04:22.728
about what the other person
is actually doing,

00:04:22.728 --> 00:04:24.964
and we just need to move
out of that space

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.899
because I think
what most people just want

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:30.002
is for us to actually
accomplish something

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:32.571
as a government
that helps working people.

00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:33.906
-You have also,

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.842
or I should say
the GOP has also promised

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:39.278
to get to the bottom
of the Biden crime family

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:42.215
and their term, not mine.
-Yeah.

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:44.616
-It does not seem
as though, you know, again,

00:04:44.616 --> 00:04:47.854
as you said, three months,
no breaking news.

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:50.956
-Yeah. I mean, I think --
they've tried, you know.

00:04:50.956 --> 00:04:54.894
They had that big
Twitter, Hunter Biden hearing

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:56.695
and they're like,
"We got him."

00:04:56.695 --> 00:05:00.099
And then the thing
about hearings is that

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:02.101
they're not Republican
press conferences.

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:05.171
You have 50 Democrats that are
also or however many Democrats

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:07.039
in the committee
that are also seated on that.

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:09.108
And they can real-time
fact-check you,

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:12.478
unlike Fox News,
as a "safe space" for them.

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:14.179
You know, you can get
fact-checked in real time.

00:05:14.179 --> 00:05:16.081
You will be debated
in real time.

00:05:16.081 --> 00:05:21.053
And they have operated
in this insular environment

00:05:21.053 --> 00:05:23.322
that affirms them,
no matter how true or false,

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:25.091
anything they say
is that now

00:05:25.091 --> 00:05:27.826
that they're actually
in a House majority

00:05:27.826 --> 00:05:29.461
and they have to
actually call hearings

00:05:29.461 --> 00:05:31.464
and they actually
have to legislate

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:34.166
and they actually have
to be called on things

00:05:34.166 --> 00:05:35.735
when they're not true,

00:05:35.735 --> 00:05:37.202
they're like, "Wait, this
doesn't feel like

00:05:37.202 --> 00:05:38.771
Tucker Carlson to me."

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:40.640
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:44.844
It's like, no, baby, this is the
U.S. House of Representatives.

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:46.512
[ Cheers and applause ]
-There you go.

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:48.348
Well, if there's any lesson

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:50.316
they take away from that,
I hope that's it.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.818
Hey, what a pleasure
to have you back here.

00:05:52.818 --> 00:05:54.887
It's always -- to have
a New Yorker here, especially

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:58.524
one -- the beautiful --
from the beautiful LaGuardia.

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:00.426
I mean, the most beautiful
airport in the whole world.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:02.094
-Look at the fountain
when you go.
-Look at the fountain.

00:06:02.094 --> 00:06:03.996
-Book your next flight.
-It's gorgeous.

00:06:03.996 --> 00:06:05.230
-It's worth flying from Europe

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:08.568
just to land at JFK, drive
to LaGuardia.

00:06:08.568 --> 00:06:10.669
Look at it. Drive back to JFK,
go back to Europe.

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:13.572
-What I will say, though,
is Moynihan Train Hall --

00:06:13.572 --> 00:06:15.341
Let's put another one
for public transit over there.

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:17.009
The new train hall, Amtrak.
I love it too.

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:19.444
-The Moynihan Train Hall is
great.

00:06:19.444 --> 00:06:20.646
This is very exciting.

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:22.114
You know, things have
really turned around

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:23.615
since you got here.
You guys, give it up for

00:06:23.615 --> 00:06:25.584
Congresswoman Alexandria
Ocasio-Cortez.

00:06:25.584 --> 00:06:27.220
-We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

